Meena dreamed of attending school, but her grandmother insisted she stay home to help with housework. While her brothers went to school, she watched from her window, counting school bells.

One day, her teacher visited their home. She explained to Meena's family about the Right to Education Act and how educating girls strengthens families. She shared stories of successful women from their village.

Slowly, her grandmother's perspective changed. Today, Meena not only attends school but ranks first in her class. The school bell now rings for her too.